nils-postcontrast-full: the third-party components in this image and their terms

Beside NILS's own code (AGPL-3.0-only, https://github.com/kineuro/nils), the
image carries:

FreeSurfer 8.2.0's parts, copied unchanged from FreeSurfer's own image
(freesurfer/freesurfer, pinned by digest in Dockerfile.full): the Python the
Synth tools run in (fspython, with its packages, less its readline module and
library, OpenCV and the spheremorph package, which none of them uses), the
scripts mri_synthseg, mri_synthstrip and mri_synthmorph with their wrappers,
the synthmorph package, SynthSeg 2.0's networks and label lists, SynthStrip's
network, SynthMorph's affine network, the MNI ICBM 2009c template folder
and FreeSurfer's colour table (FreeSurferColorLUT.txt).
They are subject to the FreeSurfer Software License Agreement. Its text, with
the opening sentence its Part B asks for, is FreeSurfer-license.txt beside
this file. Nothing else of FreeSurfer is here, and no FreeSurfer licence key.

/opt/nils-postcontrast/fs-scripts/mri_synthseg.py is FreeSurfer's
mri_synthseg changed in one line for NumPy 2; it says so at its top.

SynthSeg: Billot B, Greve DN, Puonti O, Thielscher A, Van Leemput K, Fischl B,
Dalca AV, Iglesias JE. SynthSeg: segmentation of brain MRI scans of any
contrast and resolution without retraining. Medical Image Analysis 2023.
Billot B, Magdamo C, Cheng Y, Arnold SE, Das S, Iglesias JE. Robust machine
learning segmentation for large-scale analysis of heterogeneous clinical brain
MRI datasets. PNAS 2023. Its 2.0 networks come with FreeSurfer, under the
agreement above.

SynthStrip's network (synthstrip.1.pt): Hoopes A, Mora JS, Dalca AV, Fischl B,
Hoffmann M. SynthStrip: skull-stripping for any brain image. NeuroImage 2022.
Used under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), one of the two its authors
offer (https://surfer.nmr.mgh.harvard.edu/docs/synthstrip/).

SynthMorph's affine network (synthmorph.affine.2.h5): Hoffmann M, Hoopes A,
Greve DN, Fischl B, Dalca AV. Anatomy-aware and acquisition-agnostic joint
registration with SynthMorph. Imaging Neuroscience 2024. Hoffmann M, Billot B,
Greve DN, Iglesias JE, Fischl B, Dalca AV. SynthMorph: learning
contrast-invariant registration without acquired images. IEEE Transactions on
Medical Imaging 2022. Used under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence, one of the two its authors offer
(https://synthmorph.io).

The MNI ICBM 2009c nonlinear asymmetric template: Copyright (C) 1993-2004 Louis
Collins, McConnell Brain Imaging Centre, Montreal Neurological Institute,
McGill University. Its notice is MNI-ICBM152-2009c-COPYING.txt beside this
file. Fonov VS, Evans AC, McKinstry RC, Almli CR, Collins DL. NeuroImage 2009;
Fonov V, Evans AC, Botteron K, Almli CR, McKinstry RC, Collins DL. NeuroImage
2011.

dcm2niix v1.0.20241211 (https://github.com/rordenlab/dcm2niix): its licence is
dcm2niix-license.txt beside this file.

The Apache License 2.0 (voxelmorph, neurite, TensorFlow and others among the
Python packages) is Apache-2.0.txt beside this file. Every Python package, in
FreeSurfer's Python and in /opt, carries its own licence in its dist-info
folder, and NVIDIA's CUDA libraries carry NVIDIA's terms there. NVIDIA's ptxas,
which TensorFlow's CUDA compiler wheel holds, and Triton, which PyTorch pulls,
are not in the image: no NVIDIA licence names those tools as redistributable.
